@startuml
title Realize geometry from fixed topology (priority-driven flood-fill onto macro-cells)

start
:Map each seed node to a macro-cell\nseed position (deterministic from world seed);
:Identity and target size range for every\npatch already fixed by the CSP stage -\nno legality decision left to make here;

while (any patch below its min size\nand still has claimable frontier?) is (yes)
  :Pick the patch furthest below\nits target size (priority);
  :Claim its highest-priority frontier cell\n(nearest-to-seed + deterministic jitter -\nsame ordering GrowthEngine uses today);
  note right
    Frontier is restricted to cells whose other
    touching patches are already-fixed CSP-graph
    neighbors. Legality was decided in Step 2 -
    this pass only races patches to size.
  end note
endwhile (no)

:Sweep any macro-cells still unclaimed\n(pockets left between patches);
if (unclaimed cell has an assigned\nMoore-neighbor patch?) then (yes)
  :Assign to nearest claiming patch\n(multi-source BFS - same mechanism as\ntoday's GapFiller.fillGaps);
else (no)
  :Isolated pocket with no adjacent\nclaimed patch - flag for local repair\n(caller's job, not this pass);
endif

stop
@enduml
